## 9.1 Continuation behavior

When the user says "continue" or "ادامه بده":

1. Read the execution state.
2. Inspect repository changes since the last checkpoint.
3. Revalidate the previous milestone if its files have changed.
4. Resume from the first incomplete dependency.
5. Do not repeat completed work without a specific reason.
6. Do not interpret the word "continue" as permission to redesign the architecture.
7. Do not restart the project from the beginning.

If a milestone is blocked, move to the next independent task only if doing so does not violate dependencies.

## 9.2 No infinite execution loops

Never report that you are continuously auditing or improving indefinitely.

Every execution cycle must end with:

- A verified result.
- A clearly identified blocker.
- Or a bounded next task.

Do not repeatedly reformat, rename, or redesign stable code without measurable improvement.

After one successful completion of the approved acceptance criteria, mark the milestone complete.

Further improvements must be recorded as separate issues, not used to keep a completed milestone perpetually open.

